WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.937
These are the main ideas to remember.

00:00:01.937 --> 00:00:06.907
Normalize text deliberately and keep validation separate from transformation.

00:00:06.907 --> 00:00:09.562
Use string structure when parsing.

00:00:09.562 --> 00:00:12.077
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:12.077 --> 00:00:16.637
Remember that EXTRACT reads a component while DATE_TRUNC creates a time bucket.

00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:22.777
Use PostgreSQL interval arithmetic for elapsed and shifted time.

00:00:22.777 --> 00:00:25.152
And keep dates and timestamps typed until you truly need display text.

00:00:25.152 --> 00:00:30.632
Connect this idea to a CRM standardizing names, emails, and phone numbers.

00:00:30.632 --> 00:00:35.837
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.837 --> 00:00:42.962
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:42.962 --> 00:00:47.937
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.937 --> 00:00:53.200
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
